WEBVTT

00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:13.830
You can't underestimate Mac, man.

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:16.040
You mean Mac Time?

00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:19.000
If we're talking about experience,
Liu's got the advantage,

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:21.290
but Mac's movements aren't human--

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:23.290
But Liu's on another level.

00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:27.970
He's the local champion.
He's not about to let us down!

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:38.480
Always know where your feet are and
where your opponent is at all times.

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:41.940
Looks like the champion's
progressing rather nicely.

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:44.440
After defeating "Gearless"
Joe five years ago,

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:47.070
he also won at the second Megalonia.

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:51.070
He is now truly the King of Kings.

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:54.950
He doesn't feel like he's
surpassed Yuri yet, though.

00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:57.700
Oh, he's just being modest.

00:00:57.700 --> 00:00:59.960
Undefeated since his debut match.

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:03.290
Now that he's totally overwritten
Yuri's defense record,

00:01:03.290 --> 00:01:06.550
who else could be called King right now?

00:01:08.590 --> 00:01:11.010
So what you're saying...

00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:15.050
...is that Liu's sole focus
is to surpass his mentor

00:01:15.050 --> 00:01:17.220
and Mac's not even on his radar.

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:19.980
Yeah, I couldn't say.

00:01:24.190 --> 00:01:29.400
Yuri, Mac wouldn't be considered
a standard opponent.

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:32.570
Do you two have a strategy
to counter Mac Time?

00:01:32.570 --> 00:01:35.030
You'll just have to watch the match.

00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:42.210
Speaking of not following the standard,
that reminds me of the original.

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:46.960
"Gearless" Joe.

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:51.380
He's back in town.

00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:15.900
"MEGALOBOX 2"

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:26.270
We've already got a
sparring partner set up for you.

00:03:26.270 --> 00:03:29.440
Please. I want to fight Joe again.

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:32.110
You defeated him. That's all you need.

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:36.360
Wait!

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:40.620
When I fought him, he wasn't
the same man that fought you.

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:43.580
You know that better than anyone else.

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:47.710
Apparently he's been fighting in
underground matches ever since.

00:03:47.710 --> 00:03:50.330
I can't let this opportunity slip by.

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:55.420
I'll live if he doesn't live up
to my expectations.

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:58.430
Please let me spar with Joe!

00:03:58.430 --> 00:03:59.550
Liu.

00:03:59.550 --> 00:04:02.390
Yuri came back to the Megalo-boxing world

00:04:02.390 --> 00:04:06.140
he had once left behind
to fight alongside you.

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:08.350
Did you forget that?

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:14.940
Please excuse me.

00:04:23.490 --> 00:04:28.410
This is the first time he's ever
requested anything from me.

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:34.250
His turning point in life came when he saw
the match between you and Joe.

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:39.720
I'm sure he's reaching for the stars,
but he wants to fight that Joe.

00:04:42.510 --> 00:04:47.890
He's right. The Joe he fought
wasn't the same man I fought.

00:04:47.890 --> 00:04:52.520
But despite the circumstances,
the winner is still the winner,

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:54.520
and the loser is the loser.

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:59.320
Liu's completely forgotten there
was a chance he could've lost.

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:03.370
It's arrogance.
Obsessing over foolish pride.

00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:05.370
Is that really it, though?

00:05:06.290 --> 00:05:09.040
When you continue down the road to glory,

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:12.040
you can't shake the fear that
you may lose it all someday.

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:17.880
Perhaps Liu is instinctively
feeling that with this match.

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:21.130
So he's trying to get rid of any
anxiety he might have towards Mac?

00:05:21.130 --> 00:05:25.050
You told me a while back

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:29.930
that you never once regretted the
fact that you took off your Gear

00:05:29.930 --> 00:05:33.060
to fight Joe fair and square.

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:34.400
Correct.

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:39.490
He wants to spar with Joe again so he
can push himself as far as he can

00:05:39.490 --> 00:05:41.860
and he can feel as satisfied as you do.

00:05:41.860 --> 00:05:46.160
At least, that's how I interpreted
what he was saying.

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:04.050
Hello, there. Long time no see.

00:06:05.930 --> 00:06:09.600
You didn't retire to become
a carpenter, did you?

00:06:10.550 --> 00:06:15.560
Team Nowhere

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:15.480
Are you actually trying
to rebuild this place?

00:06:17.900 --> 00:06:19.440
For real?

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:26.740
This is the place where you were also
looking after a bunch of orphans, right?

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:30.870
Is that why you agreed to
fight with me back then?

00:06:30.870 --> 00:06:34.710
What did you want?
I'm sure you can see that I'm busy.

00:06:36.920 --> 00:06:42.260
I have a job offer for you.
I want you to be my sparring partner.

00:06:42.260 --> 00:06:43.920
Why me?

00:06:45.050 --> 00:06:47.680
Does Yuri know about this?

00:06:47.680 --> 00:06:49.930
Yuri's got nothing to do with this.

00:06:49.930 --> 00:06:52.520
This is between you and me.

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:55.390
You owe me.

00:06:55.390 --> 00:06:59.310
First, you got into that ring
in the worst possible condition.

00:06:59.310 --> 00:07:04.740
Second, you underestimated me
because it was an exhibition match.

00:07:04.740 --> 00:07:06.780
I'm not gonna make any excuses.

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:08.160
I apologize.

00:07:09.950 --> 00:07:12.490
Well, that sure was an empty apology.

00:07:12.490 --> 00:07:17.620
After all this time, I'm still
stuck chasing your shadow.

00:07:17.620 --> 00:07:21.920
It doesn't matter how many times I win.
They say the same thing.

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:25.340
It's because I'm Yuri's student.

00:07:25.340 --> 00:07:31.010
You guys got to give your all that match
and probably don't have any regrets.

00:07:31.010 --> 00:07:34.890
But I'm still suffering because of it.

00:07:34.890 --> 00:07:39.560
You're basically digging your heel
into my foot while apologizing.

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:46.280
I don't mind making it up to you.

00:07:46.280 --> 00:07:49.450
But fighting me in my current state...

00:07:50.820 --> 00:07:54.290
It's really not that deep.

00:07:54.290 --> 00:07:57.790
Think of it as a break from your carpentry

00:07:57.790 --> 00:08:00.670
and show me what you've
been doing on the road.

00:08:03.170 --> 00:08:06.220
You abandoned everything and ran away,

00:08:06.220 --> 00:08:09.300
but you still couldn't
abandon Megalo-boxing.

00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:18.060
The day you finally leave
that ring for good

00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:20.520
is the day you'll be
parting with this world.

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:23.150
Am I wrong?

00:08:29.860 --> 00:08:33.410
IMA ranking 127.

00:08:33.410 --> 00:08:38.790
Back then, Mac couldn't
control his emotions.

00:08:38.790 --> 00:08:41.540
His wins and losses continued
to outdo each other.

00:08:41.540 --> 00:08:43.790
No one knew he existed.

00:08:43.790 --> 00:08:46.340
He was just another boxer
stuck in mediocrity.

00:08:47.710 --> 00:08:52.010
After retiring due to his
wife Maya's pregnancy,

00:08:52.010 --> 00:08:54.010
Mac became a police officer.

00:08:58.980 --> 00:09:02.650
Later on, he got caught up
in a gang dispute,

00:09:02.650 --> 00:09:07.480
and became a local hero after
saving many of the local citizens.

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:10.110
But he paid a heavy price.

00:09:12.610 --> 00:09:14.870
As he was trying to save a
child who had gotten away,

00:09:14.870 --> 00:09:18.250
he was hit by a stray bullet and
suffered a spinal cord injury.

00:09:18.250 --> 00:09:22.670
The price he would end up
paying is total paralysis.

00:09:24.130 --> 00:09:28.380
Mac remained in a coma for quite some time

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:31.010
but then a ray of hope
shone down upon him.

00:09:32.340 --> 00:09:34.850
And that man was...

00:09:34.850 --> 00:09:39.480
The man who brought upon a medical
revolution with neuro-engineering...

00:09:39.480 --> 00:09:41.850
The young, genius entrepreneur...

00:09:41.850 --> 00:09:46.270
The CEO of ROSCO, Ryugo Sakuma.

00:09:46.270 --> 00:09:49.230
We have always believed
that the latest technology

00:09:49.230 --> 00:09:54.030
would shine the brightest
in the medical field.

00:09:54.030 --> 00:09:56.830
The ability to regain sight and hearing.

00:09:56.830 --> 00:09:59.120
Recovering from memory disorders.

00:09:59.120 --> 00:10:01.000
Every time we came up with a new product,

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:05.290
we concentrated on finding a new cure.

00:10:06.290 --> 00:10:08.420
And the product that ROSCO created

00:10:08.420 --> 00:10:13.220
by bringing together all of the latest
technology in order to save Mac was...

00:10:13.220 --> 00:10:15.800
The Brain Encoding System.

00:10:15.800 --> 00:10:18.810
BES for short.

00:10:18.810 --> 00:10:21.430
The chip that is implanted
into his brain sends a signal

00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:25.230
to the artificial nerve tract
made up of Assisting Gears

00:10:25.230 --> 00:10:27.360
allowing him to move freely.

00:10:28.690 --> 00:10:31.990
The one who assisted us in the BES Project

00:10:31.990 --> 00:10:35.910
is none other than the CEO of the
Shirato Group, Yukiko Shirato.

00:10:37.370 --> 00:10:40.660
After coming onboard with
Sakuma's idea and project,

00:10:40.660 --> 00:10:42.660
Shirato had been assisting
with the creation

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:45.210
of the Assisting Gears from the
creation of the brain chip stage

00:10:45.210 --> 00:10:48.880
and offered technology
from her own company.

00:10:48.880 --> 00:10:52.590
And then Mac...

00:10:52.590 --> 00:10:58.930
At first, I was just thankful
to live a normal life again.

00:10:58.930 --> 00:11:02.770
But the more control I regained
over my body, I became greedy.

00:11:04.600 --> 00:11:08.360
And that's when Mr. Sakuma asked,

00:11:08.360 --> 00:11:12.650
"Have you thought about giving
Megalo-boxing another try?"

00:11:12.650 --> 00:11:17.610
Mac would reenter the ring
as a boxer under ROSCO,

00:11:17.610 --> 00:11:19.030
and was a completely different man.

00:11:19.030 --> 00:11:23.370
He could now control his emotions
and won match after match.

00:11:25.710 --> 00:11:27.540
Even when he's at a disadvantage,

00:11:27.540 --> 00:11:30.540
he was always able to
turn the tables in the end.

00:11:30.540 --> 00:11:34.050
The people started calling
this phenomenon... Mac Time.

00:11:34.050 --> 00:11:35.670
Whenever the odds weren't in my favor,

00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:40.890
I used to attack recklessly
to get rid of my fear.

00:11:40.890 --> 00:11:43.680
But that's not necessary anymore.

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:45.350
When I get in the zone,

00:11:45.350 --> 00:11:50.230
I'm naturally able to perform my best
and my opponent just goes down.

00:11:52.070 --> 00:11:56.530
I hesitated getting back into
the ring because of my family.

00:11:56.530 --> 00:12:01.910
But my son didn't know
about my time as a fighter.

00:12:01.910 --> 00:12:06.620
I don't want to be the champ
or anything that grand.

00:12:06.620 --> 00:12:10.420
I just wanted him to see
his father in that ring.

00:12:10.420 --> 00:12:11.420
I see.

00:12:11.420 --> 00:12:14.420
How did you feel about this, Maya?

00:12:14.420 --> 00:12:16.550
Were you nervous at all?

00:12:16.550 --> 00:12:19.300
I'd be lying if I said I wasn't,

00:12:19.300 --> 00:12:23.390
but I wanted to respect his
wishes as much as possible.

00:12:23.390 --> 00:12:25.810
Your title match is coming up.

00:12:25.810 --> 00:12:27.810
I'm filled with gratitude.

00:12:27.810 --> 00:12:32.900
Especially for my wife.
As well as Mr. Sakuma...

00:12:32.900 --> 00:12:36.860
For me... winning that match...

00:12:39.820 --> 00:12:42.120
That's...

00:12:42.120 --> 00:12:46.250
The only way I can repay them right now.

00:12:54.460 --> 00:12:59.090
I don't want anything in return.
I even told him that.

00:12:59.090 --> 00:13:03.260
He basically helped me grow.

00:13:03.260 --> 00:13:06.060
"People who reach their
full potential are beautiful."

00:13:06.060 --> 00:13:07.810
Remember when you said that?

00:13:07.810 --> 00:13:09.520
Did I?

00:13:09.520 --> 00:13:13.270
Because there's nothing but blood,
sweat, and tears in the shadows.

00:13:15.480 --> 00:13:20.990
Did you watch Yuri train like this
when he was still fighting?

00:13:20.990 --> 00:13:25.160
He always preferred to be alone.

00:13:25.160 --> 00:13:27.870
Who are you rooting for
in the upcoming match?

00:13:27.870 --> 00:13:31.620
Yuri's prized pupil Liu, or...

00:13:31.620 --> 00:13:36.380
My apologies. I'm sure your not
interested in the match anymore.

00:13:36.380 --> 00:13:41.010
It's true that our company isn't
involved in Megalo-boxing anymore

00:13:41.010 --> 00:13:44.510
but it's not because we don't
see potential in Gears anymore.

00:13:44.510 --> 00:13:47.100
Especially for the medical field.

00:13:47.100 --> 00:13:51.350
If we can prove how much
potential BES has in this match,

00:13:51.350 --> 00:13:54.310
my answer is that I will
be rooting for Mac.

00:13:56.820 --> 00:14:00.360
People cannot move forward without hope.

00:14:05.820 --> 00:14:09.290
Mac is the light of hope.

00:14:10.870 --> 00:14:13.960
So many people who can't
escape from the darkness

00:14:13.960 --> 00:14:16.540
are waiting for BES to become available.

00:14:16.540 --> 00:14:20.380
And we can make that happen, Yukiko.

00:14:20.380 --> 00:14:21.550
Indeed.

00:14:39.480 --> 00:14:42.820
Thanks for coming, Mister Joe!

00:14:45.860 --> 00:14:47.660
Glad to help.

00:14:52.160 --> 00:14:54.080
Hey there, old timer.

00:14:55.370 --> 00:14:57.460
You'll find what you need in the back.

00:15:01.050 --> 00:15:04.680
Well, I see you haven't changed, Yuri.

00:15:14.020 --> 00:15:16.310
Are you all warmed up?

00:15:17.650 --> 00:15:19.650
I'm ready when you are.

00:15:38.170 --> 00:15:40.500
I guess he's going for the counter.

00:15:40.500 --> 00:15:41.960
Yes.

00:15:41.960 --> 00:15:44.380
Liu, don't hold back!

00:15:53.390 --> 00:15:55.270
Shut up!

00:15:56.850 --> 00:15:58.350
Seriously.

00:15:58.350 --> 00:16:00.860
That's why I said you shouldn't come.

00:16:00.860 --> 00:16:02.480
But...

00:16:02.480 --> 00:16:06.240
You don't want to see
Joe all banged up, do you?

00:16:06.240 --> 00:16:09.200
But they just started.

00:16:15.870 --> 00:16:18.870
Nothing's harsher than reality.

00:16:21.460 --> 00:16:26.090
Let's stop, Jimmy. Any more is just...

00:16:26.090 --> 00:16:27.840
Yuri.

00:16:27.840 --> 00:16:29.840
Look at his eyes.

00:16:35.430 --> 00:16:39.270
You're... an illusion that I created.

00:16:53.700 --> 00:16:55.540
That look in his eyes...

00:16:55.540 --> 00:16:59.460
...just proves that he hasn't lost
his fighting spirit in the least.

00:17:14.760 --> 00:17:18.390
You're going to have regrets if you don't
fight under the same circumstances.

00:17:48.510 --> 00:17:50.590
Ow...

00:17:50.590 --> 00:17:53.510
Hey, guys! Thanks for the show!

00:17:56.140 --> 00:17:57.390
This way!

00:17:59.640 --> 00:18:01.560
What're they doing here?

00:18:03.350 --> 00:18:06.520
Sorry. They're ol' buddies of mine.

00:18:06.520 --> 00:18:10.780
It's fine. It's all thanks to him
that I'm fighting you right now.

00:18:12.150 --> 00:18:14.160
Looks like they got away.

00:18:16.160 --> 00:18:19.200
Looks like Liu was able to get over this.

00:18:21.000 --> 00:18:22.210
Yes.

00:18:28.590 --> 00:18:31.840
Once I finish my match
with Mac, you're next.

00:18:33.180 --> 00:18:34.590
I'm honored.

00:18:34.590 --> 00:18:36.390
You think I'm joking.

00:18:36.390 --> 00:18:38.600
That's not it.

00:18:38.600 --> 00:18:42.310
I just have some stuff
I've still gotta do.

00:18:42.310 --> 00:18:46.770
Got it. When you're done with that,
let's meet in the ring again.

00:18:46.770 --> 00:18:47.820
I'll be waiting for you.

00:18:58.320 --> 00:19:00.700
"Affordable Chinese Food Ichibanya"

00:18:59.910 --> 00:19:03.310
"The champ dominated
the first half of the match

00:19:00.700 --> 00:19:03.200
Closed Today

00:19:03.910 --> 00:19:08.040
but 'Gearless' Joe turned the
tables with his famous counter.

00:19:08.040 --> 00:19:11.550
Is he getting ready to
come out of retirement?"

00:19:11.550 --> 00:19:12.840
Seriously?

00:19:12.840 --> 00:19:15.590
How can you even write this shit?

00:19:16.680 --> 00:19:19.810
I may have embellished a little,
but I definitely didn't lie, did I?

00:19:19.810 --> 00:19:21.430
It was amazing!

00:19:21.430 --> 00:19:25.140
It was like the Joe that we
know was back in that ring.

00:19:25.140 --> 00:19:26.350
Keh.

00:19:26.350 --> 00:19:28.360
He just got lucky.

00:19:30.440 --> 00:19:32.070
First of all,

00:19:32.070 --> 00:19:34.530
you said you had a great idea
on how we can make him look

00:19:34.530 --> 00:19:35.610
like the fool that he is!

00:19:35.610 --> 00:19:36.950
This is the exact opposite!

00:19:36.950 --> 00:19:40.700
Er, let's just go with the flow here.

00:19:40.700 --> 00:19:43.700
You know, enemies one day,
friends the next.

00:19:45.080 --> 00:19:47.040
Please.

00:19:47.040 --> 00:19:51.210
Says the guy who'll betray us at the
drop of a hat if money's involved.

00:19:51.210 --> 00:19:54.670
Says the guy who chased
away Joe in the first place.

00:19:54.670 --> 00:19:56.470
They also say, "Your enemies
aren't always your enemies,

00:19:56.470 --> 00:19:58.840
and your friends aren't
always your friends!"

00:20:03.310 --> 00:20:05.890
Santa! Santa!

00:20:04.560 --> 00:20:08.900
What the heck are you doing?! Uh, Santa?

00:20:07.350 --> 00:20:08.900
Hey, Sachio!

00:20:08.900 --> 00:20:10.940
At least I didn't slug him.

00:20:12.440 --> 00:20:16.310
"The Champion Liu's Secret Sparring Session?!
Is the Legendary Boxer Making a
Comeback After Disappearing for 5 Years?!"

00:20:27.040 --> 00:20:28.500
Daddy?

00:20:28.500 --> 00:20:30.670
Why are you smiling?

00:20:37.670 --> 00:20:42.140
I guess Sachio and Oicho
didn't come after all.

00:20:42.140 --> 00:20:45.600
Just look at these awesome
seats we got for free!

00:20:45.600 --> 00:20:48.810
They need to get
over themselves, seriously.

00:20:48.810 --> 00:20:52.440
You guys don't have to be
here either, you know?

00:20:52.440 --> 00:20:54.360
No one's twisting my arm...

00:20:56.940 --> 00:20:59.740
I don't care about any of that.

00:20:59.740 --> 00:21:02.830
If I can make a quick buck
off of you, I sure the hell will.

00:21:04.700 --> 00:21:05.910
Sure.

00:21:09.500 --> 00:21:10.710
Ma'am.

00:21:13.250 --> 00:21:15.000
Brother.

00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:17.880
It's been a while, Yukiko.

00:21:20.090 --> 00:21:25.260
I feel like I'm dreaming.
I can't believe I'm actually here.

00:21:25.260 --> 00:21:28.770
You're the one who allowed
us to dream again.

00:21:29.850 --> 00:21:33.150
I'm not the only one who wants
to see how it turns out anymore.

00:21:54.000 --> 00:21:56.840
Ranking 2nd in the IMA ranking!

00:21:58.260 --> 00:22:01.260
Representing Sons of ROSCO...

00:22:01.260 --> 00:22:08.810
The Public Hero... Mac Rosario!

00:22:11.520 --> 00:22:17.020
Our hero that made a miraculous
comeback is now entering the ring!

00:22:17.020 --> 00:22:21.450
Will we be able to witness Mac Time
